/**
@page working_with_colors Working with Colors

Throughout `Xlsxwriter++` colors are specified using a HTML style RGB
integer value. For example with a Format object:

@code
  format->set_font_color(xwpp::color_t{0x3030E0});
@endcode

`Xlsxwriter++` support color defined by the three RBG components or CMYK
components too.

@code
  format->set_font_color(xwpp::color_t::rgb(0x30, 0x30, 0xE0));
  format->set_font_color(xwpp::color_t::cmyk(79, 79, 0, 12));
@endcode

For convenience a limited number of color names are supported:

@code
  format->set_font_color(xwpp::color_t::red());
@endcode

The color names and corresponding `RRGGBB` value are shown below:

| Color                                       | Functions               | Value         |
| ------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------- |
| <span style="color:#000000">Black</span>    | `%color_t::black()`     | `0x000000`    |
| <span style="color:#0000FF">Blue</span>     | `%color_t::blue()`      | `0x0000FF`    |
| <span style="color:#800000">Brown</span>    | `%color_t::brown()`     | `0x800000`    |
| <span style="color:#00FFFF">Cyan</span>     | `%color_t::cyan()`      | `0x00FFFF`    |
| <span style="color:#808080">Gray</span>     | `%color_t::gray()`      | `0x808080`    |
| <span style="color:#008000">Green</span>    | `%color_t::green()`     | `0x008000`    |
| <span style="color:#00FF00">Lime</span>     | `%color_t::lime()`      | `0x00FF00`    |
| <span style="color:#FF00FF">Magenta</span>  | `%color_t::magenta()`   | `0xFF00FF`    |
| <span style="color:#000080">Navy</span>     | `%color_t::navy()`      | `0x000080`    |
| <span style="color:#FF6600">Orange</span>   | `%color_t::orange()`    | `0xFF6600`    |
| <span style="color:#FF00FF">Pink</span>     | `%color_t::pink()`      | `0xFF00FF`    |
| <span style="color:#800080">Purple</span>   | `%color_t::purple()`    | `0x800080`    |
| <span style="color:#FF0000">Red</span>      | `%color_t::red()`       | `0xFF0000`    |
| <span style="color:#C0C0C0">Silver</span>   | `%color_t::silver()`    | `0xC0C0C0`    |
| <span style="color:#FFFFFF">White</span>    | `%color_t::white()`     | `0xFFFFFF`    |
| <span style="color:#FFFF00">Yellow</span>   | `%color_t::yellow()`    | `0xFFFF00`    |

Next: @ref working_with_formulas

*/
